    "result_text": "All 42 tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented optional, region-aware postcode validation for owners on `POST /api/owners`, keeping the request contract backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract / schema**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property (4-digit `^[0-9]{4}$`, `example: '2000'`) to the `OwnerFields` schema, so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` gain `getPostcode()`/`setPostcode()` and it's returned on GET.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field with `@Column` and getter/setter (MapStruct maps it by name on both `toOwner` and `toOwnerDto`, so it's stored and returned).\n- Added a `postcode` column to all four dialect schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\n**Validation (OfficeFloor function pipeline)**\n- New `owner/ValidatePostcode.java` \u2014 a step that skips when postcode is absent/blank; otherwise requires four digits and, for a known city region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), an in-range value. Unknown-region cities accept any 4-digit postcode. Rejects via a checked `InvalidPostcodeException`.\n- New `escalation/InvalidPostcodeException.java` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler.java` (responds 400 with `{\"errors\":[\"postcode\"]}`) + the matching `officefloor/escalation/...InvalidPostcodeException.yml`.\n- Wired `validatePostcode` into `owners.POST.yml` right after `validate` (before the transaction begins, so an invalid body is a clean 400).\n- `owner/ApplyOwner.java` \u2014 also sets postcode on the PUT path so updates store it.\n\nThe Cp29 tests (stores a valid postcode, accepts an owner without one, rejects a malformed `\"12\"` with 400) and all other existing acceptance tests pass.",
